=== ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS ===
  • Data seam: own protocol `AuditReplayAuditSource` + `InMemoryAuditReplayAuditSource` (NO `import Shared`) so the
    surface host-compiles WITHOUT the unstaged KMP xcframework. The web `AuditPanel` is presentational (props
    `rows`/`loading`/`scopedDlqId`); the native surface elevates those props into the P1/S8 cache-then-network state
    holder (the DLQ replay-audit feed) and the view performs ZERO HTTP. A `AuditPanelModel(rows:loading:scopedDlqId:)`
    web-prop initializer preserves the exact `<AuditPanel rows loading scopedDlqId/>` call site.
  • Load state: self-contained `AuditPanelLoadState` + `AuditPanelError` mirroring the facade `LoadableState`/
    `FacadeError` SHAPE (cached-behind-refresh, ADR-013 stale, offline-keeps-cache, retryable) — so the production
    binding is a 1:1 map and every branch is unit-testable. The web shell only branches on loading/`rows.length`;
    the resolver is a documented SUPERSET adding the prompt's stale/offline/error chrome.
  • i18n: per-surface `.strings` table + `AuditPanelStrings` facade (NSLocalizedString tableName + value fallback) —
    parallel-safe across the concurrent slots; the shared Localizable.xcstrings is NOT edited (Honesty rule 7).
  • Table: hand-composed (not the shared `TSDataTable`) because TSDataTable takes main-catalog `LocalizedStringKey`
    headers (no per-surface fallback) and always renders a selection column the read-only audit log has not — the
    same disposition the 0069 NotificationStatsWidget log records for its log table. The shared `TSTone` (result
    chip color) and `TSSkeleton` (loading) ARE reused, and the empty state is the shared `ContentUnavailableView`
    pattern with facade `Text` (web `EmptyState`).
  • Telemetry: REUSES the canonical `DashboardWidgetTelemetryEvent` / `DashboardWidgetTelemetrySink` /
    `BufferedDashboardWidgetTelemetry` (Sources/DashboardWidgets/BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift), whose doc string
    declares the PII-free name/surface pair is "all a feature surface is allowed to construct" — the app-wide P1/S11
    diagnostics seam. `AuditPanel.viewOpenedEvent == .viewOpened(surface:"AuditPanel")`, emitted on `.task`.
  • Proto/units note: the result tokens are stable string codes (web `DLQReplayResult`); no unit-suffixed fields are
    involved, so the Phase-48 SI-canonical rules do not apply to this surface.

